    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d762">

                <pb facs="0859" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/10089</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-27T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 27, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3.20 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4947. Your 3844, September 18, 4 p. m. Reply of Foreign Office to representations
                    transmitted by despatch 4706. In reply to oral representations Foreign Office
                    unofficially informs that British Government not willing to grant facilities for
                    any needles of German origin since needles can mostly be procured from United
                    Kingdom.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
